.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ngx 1  "ngx 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
ngx \- Manage nginx sites and Let\*(Aqs Encrypt certificates
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBngx\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Manage nginx sites and Let\*(Aqs Encrypt certificates.
.PP
Run without a command to open the full\-screen dashboard. Every change is backed up, validated with `nginx \-t`, rolled back on failure and followed by a reload that waits until nginx has picked up the new configuration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ngx\-ls(1)
List sites with status, SSL, renewal, ports and errors
.TP
ngx\-show(1)
Show everything about one site: SSL, routing, backend process, locations, logs, traffic
.TP
ngx\-add(1)
Create and enable a new site (asks for anything not given as a flag)
.TP
ngx\-edit(1)
Change a site\*(Aqs settings: same questions as `add`, pre\-filled with the current values
.TP
ngx\-rm(1)
Remove a site\*(Aqs configuration (a backup is kept)
.TP
ngx\-enable(1)
Enable a disabled site
.TP
ngx\-disable(1)
Disable a site without deleting it (`ngx enable` brings it back with the same ID)
.TP
ngx\-cert(1)
Certificates: info, issue, renew, auto\-renewal on/off (wraps certbot)
.TP
ngx\-logs(1)
Show a site\*(Aqs access log (or error log with \-e)
.TP
ngx\-test(1)
Validate the nginx configuration (`nginx \-t`)
.TP
ngx\-reload(1)
Validate, then reload nginx (waits until the new config is live)
.TP
ngx\-doctor(1)
Check the environment: nginx, certbot, layout, renewal timer, permissions
.TP
ngx\-init(1)
Create sites\-available/ + sites\-enabled/ and include them from nginx.conf (Arch, RHEL, …)
.TP
ngx\-tui(1)
Full\-screen dashboard (also the default when no command is given)
.TP
ngx\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  ngx                      open the dashboard
  ngx ls                   list sites
  ngx show 4               details of site #4
  sudo ngx add             create a site (interactive)
  sudo ngx edit api.example.com \-\-local 8081 \-y

Docs: docs/README.md · man ngx
